task.refactor.new_learning_process_for_video (completed) {
  major refactor {
    - when learning a youtube video:
      - download the youtube video transcript to <video_id_hash>.transcript
      - generate trunks of the transcript similar to the ones in /news learning
      - DO NOT need to generate the .rewrite files and .embedding
  }

  create youtube_video_learning_migration.py {
    - remote all the existing .embedding, .trunk, .rewrite files in {directory_of_this_prompt}/../.chat/youtube_transcripts directory
    - examine all *.transcript files, generate new trunk files similar to the news
  }

  Implemented:
  youtube_video_learn.py
  - STEPS is now fetch_youtube_transcript.py -> create_trunks.py. Rewrite and
    embeddings are no longer part of learning.
  create_trunks.py
  - Reads <video>.transcript (falling back to the video id when a title is
    missing), strips caption speaker markers, splits the raw transcript into
    sentence-aligned paragraphs, and writes one overview trunk (index 0) plus
    one paragraph trunk per chunk, matching news learning. Re-learning removes
    that video's old trunks first.
  youtube_video_learning_migration.py
  - Removes every .embedding (including .paragraph.embedding), .trunk, and
    .rewrite file in .chat/youtube_transcripts, then rebuilds news-style trunks
    from every existing .transcript. Supports --dry-run, continues past a bad
    transcript, and exits non-zero if any transcript fails.
  app/chat_server.py
  - Learn progress weights match the two remaining steps.
    video_is_learned() now requires the transcript plus at least one trunk
    instead of a .rewrite file.

  Verified:
  - py_compile passes for the changed Python files; a temp-dir run built 34
    trunks (overview + 33 paragraphs) from a real transcript.
  - Ran the migration on the live corpus: 23,414 embedding files, 11,707 old
    trunks, and 546 rewrite files removed; 19,482 news-style trunks rebuilt
    for all 546 transcripts, with no failures.
}

