task.refactor.youtube_search_improvement_using_google_rss (completed) {
  refactor the /youtube search command:
  example: when i search "jensen huang" {
    - result: use "https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=site:youtube.com+jensen+huang&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en"
    - analyse {result}, only return list of results that has <source url="https://www.youtube.com">YouTube</source>

    - do not return the video image, simply return list of video url and video title is ok 
  }

  Implemented:
  youtube_news_search.py (new)
  - /youtube search now queries Google News RSS with site:youtube.com,
    hl=en-US, gl=US, ceid=US:en instead of YouTube's InnerTube search.
  - Only feed items whose <source> is YouTube are kept (case-insensitive
    source name plus youtube.com/m.youtube.com/music.youtube.com URL).
  - Google News redirect links are resolved through the batchexecute exchange
    to real YouTube watch URLs, so the returned result is a playable video.
    Resolved links are cached in .chat/youtube_news_links.json so the "More"
    button and background prefetch do not repeat the exchange.
  - Results contain only the video id, title, watch URL, and the feed's
    publish date; no thumbnail, duration, or caption lookup is performed.
  - Supports --json, --progressive-json, --limit, and --exclude so the
    existing /youtube search cache, "More" button, Summary, Learn, and
    Bookmark actions keep working unchanged.
  app/chat_server.py
  - _youtube_search_command now runs youtube_news_search.py and no longer
    applies the old 5-60 minute/English-caption filters for this command.
  - _normalize_youtube_items carries the no_thumbnail flag, and the /youtube
    search messages/headings describe the Google News RSS source.
  - search_youtube.py is unchanged and still powers /youtube learn_topic.
  app/chat.html
  - Video search cards honor no_thumbnail, so Google News results show a
    compact title/url card instead of a generated thumbnail. Cards without a
    known date no longer print "Release date unavailable".

  Verified: `python3 youtube_news_search.py --json --limit 4 -- "jensen
  huang"` returns four resolved youtube.com/watch?v=... URLs with titles and
  dates; an --exclude follow-up returns the next unseen videos. Python syntax
  checks pass for youtube_news_search.py and app/chat_server.py, and the
  browser script passes `node --check`.
}

