task (completed) {
  bug:
  now when i click "learn" in youtube video, it fails to fetch youtube transcript, why? please fix it

  Root cause:
  youtube-transcript-api raises RequestBlocked/IpBlocked on this network, and
  the learn pipeline had no fallback, so fetch_youtube_transcript.py exited
  before rewrite/trunks/embeddings ever ran.

  Implemented:
  fetch_youtube_transcript.py
  - Added a provider chain: youtube-transcript-api first, then a yt-dlp
  fallback. The fallback tries the ios/web_embedded/mweb/android_vr player
  clients and uses --ignore-no-formats-error, so captions are retrievable
  even when YouTube returns "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot" to the
  transcript API.
  - Parses yt-dlp's json3 captions (VTT as fallback) into the same plain-text
  format the rest of the pipeline already expects.
  - Added caching: an existing .transcript is reused, and an existing .title
  is reused, so retries and the learn pipeline are idempotent and do not
  hit YouTube or Ollama again.
  - Added opt-in proxy support (YT_PROXY_URL, WEBSHARE_PROXY_USERNAME/
  WEBSHARE_PROXY_PASSWORD) and opt-in yt-dlp cookies
  (YT_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER, YT_COOKIES_FILE).
  - Saves the transcript before calling Ollama, so a model/title failure no
  longer discards a successful fetch, and reports one concise error with
  the blocking hint plus both provider failures.

  Verified with the blocked network that originally failed: the direct API
  reports "blocked", the yt-dlp ios client downloads json3 captions, and the
  transcript + 20-word title are written successfully. A second run completes
  from cache in ~0.15 s.
}

task (completed) {
  bug:
  when clicking on the "More" button under the list of youtube video, no videos are loaded

  Implemented:
  search_youtube.py
  - Unchanged; the progressive candidate event already contains the next
  duration-filtered videos even when caption verification cannot finish.

  app/chat_server.py
  - `_run_youtube_search` can now fall back to the candidate list when every
  English-caption lookup fails (for example when YouTube blocks caption
  requests). It also reports `captions_unverified` to the caller.
  - The `/youtube search` fallback path seeds the per-keyword cache with the
  candidate cards that were just painted, instead of leaving the cache
  empty.
  - Background prefetch and `/api/youtube_more` use the candidate fallback,
  so "More" returns the next unseen videos rather than an empty page when
  caption checks are blocked.

  app/chat.html
  - `loadMoreVideos` preserves/sets the unverified-caption state reported by
  the server, so the list label stays accurate after loading more cards.
}

task (completed) {
  currently, using youtube search <words> loads the list of video really fast, but when clicking on the "More" button, the video list is loading very slowly, please speed it up

  Implemented:
  search_youtube.py
  - Added `--exclude <video ids>`. Excluded ids are dropped while the
  candidate pool is collected, so caption checks are spent only on new
  videos instead of re-verifying the page the user already sees.
  - Candidate limits grow with the excluded set, so excluding a long list
  cannot starve the "More" page of candidates.

  app/chat_server.py
  - After the first /youtube page is rendered, a daemon thread warms the
  per-keyword cache to ~37 results in the background. The next "More"
  clicks are then served from memory with no YouTube round-trip.
  - "More" now returns cached unseen videos immediately when available,
  waits briefly for an in-progress prefetch instead of starting a
  duplicate search, and otherwise fetches only the missing unseen videos
  with `--exclude`.
  - Cache growth appends deduplicated results, preserving the newest-first
  order, and keeps prefetching after each "More" so later clicks stay fast.
}

task (completed) {
  for youtube video player, make it so that it can maximize and resume to the default size

  Implemented:
  app/chat.html
  - Added a "⛶" maximize control in the top-right corner of the embedded
  YouTube player inside the /youtube search modal.
  - Clicking it toggles `.video-player.is-maximized`, which pins the player to
  the viewport (`position: fixed; inset: 12px`) with the rest of the page
  dimmed, and clicking the "🗗" control (or pressing Escape) restores the
  modal's default player size.
  - The iframe is only resized, never reloaded, so playback continues from the
  same position across maximize/restore.
  - Escape restores a maximized player first; a second Escape then closes the
  modal as before (capture-phase handler, so it beats the existing shortcut).
  - Maximized state is reset whenever the modal is opened or closed.
}

